cache:query:What is the story of Cain, including his background as the son of Adam and Eve and the events involving his offering, his conflict with Abel, and the consequences described in Genesis?
$982
Cain was the first son of Adam and Eve, born after they â€œknewâ€ one another (the first â€œseedâ€ of the couple)â€¯[chunk-41]. He worked the soil as a â€œhusbandman,â€ while his brother Abel tended sheepâ€¯[chunk-41].  

When the time came to bring gifts to the Lord, Cain offered â€œthe fruits of the earthâ€â€¯[chunk-42], whereas Abel offered â€œthe firstlings of his flockâ€ and their fat, which earned the Lordâ€™s favorable regardâ€¯[chunk-42].  

Because God favored Abelâ€™s offering, tension arose between the brothers, and Cain killed Abelâ€”â€œthe seed for Abel, whom Cain slewâ€â€¯[chunk-54].  

The murder led to further developments in the family line: after Abelâ€™s death, Eve later bore another son, Seth, whom she named â€œGod hath given me another seed for Abelâ€â€¯[chunk-54].  

Thus, Genesis presents Cain as Adam and Eveâ€™s first son, his agricultural offering that was rejected, his killing of Abel, and the subsequent birth of Seth as a replacement.
