cache:query:what is the story of cain
$641
Cain was the first son of Adam and Eve (Genesisâ€¯4:1) and worked as a husbandman, while his brother Abel was a shepherd (chunkâ€‘41).  Out of jealousy he killed Abel, and when God asked him â€œWhere is thy brother Abel?â€ Cain replied, â€œI know not; am I my brotherâ€™s keeper?â€â€¯God then said that the blood of Abel cried out from the earth and pronounced a curse on Cain, condemning him to be a fugitive on the earth (chunkâ€‘45).  After this, Cain left the presence of the Lord, settled as a wanderer on the east side of Eden, took a wife, and they bore a son named Henoch; Cain built a city and named it after his son (chunkâ€‘49).
$4
