cache:query:What happened in chapter 3?
$843
Chapterâ€¯3 describes the temptation, the fall, and the immediate aftermath.  
- God had warned that the fruit of the tree in the middle of Paradise should not be eaten or touched, lest one die; the serpent contradicted this, telling the woman she would not die and that eating would open her eyes and make her â€œas Godsâ€ (knowing good and evil)ã€chunk-29ã€‘.  
- The woman saw the treeâ€™s fruit was pleasing and ate it, gave some to her husband, and he also ate. Their eyes were opened, they realized they were naked, and they sewed fig leaves together to make apronsã€chunk-30ã€‘.  
- Hearing the Lord God walking in Paradise, Adam and his wife hid among the trees. The Lord called to Adam, asking â€œWhere art thou?â€ Adam replied that he heard Godâ€™s voice, was afraid because he was naked, and therefore hid himselfã€chunk-33ã€‘.
