$1211
{"role": "assistant", "content": "**Definition**  \n*A man* (or *human*) is a being created by God. According to the text, God fashioned man from the dust of the earth and breathed a living soul into him. Man exists in two genders\u2014male and female\u2014and is made in the *image of God*.\n\n**Key Details**  \n1. **Creation** \u2013 God formed man from the slime of the earth and gave him life by breathing into him the breath of life, turning the body into a *living soul*\u3010chunk-19\u3011.  \n2. **Image of God** \u2013 The likeness God places in humans is not in the physical body but in the soul. This soul is a spiritual substance that possesses *understanding* and *free will*, reflecting God\u2019s own nature\u3010chunk-12\u3011.  \n3. **Dual Gender** \u2013 God created both male and female, naming them Adam at the time of their creation\u3010chunk-55\u3011.  \n4. **Plurality of God** \u2013 God\u2019s use of the plural pronoun hints at a plurality of persons within the Deity, which is reflected in the human image\u3010chunk-12\u3011.\n\nIn short, a man is a spiritually endowed, free\u2011willed human created by God, made in God\u2019s image, and existing in both male and female forms."}
